[0.081, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G-\u001b[5GManifest's market, economy,\u001b[33Gobservations\u001b[46Gand\u001b[50Gcompany\u001b[58Gare\u001b[62Gabout\u001b[68G3\u001b[70Gto\u001b[73G5%\u001b[76Gtogether.\u001b[86GThe\u001b[90Glargest\u001b[98Gof\u001b[101Gthem,\u001b[107G\u001b[38;2;177;185;249mTrade::Step\u001b[39m,\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bis 1.7%.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B-\u001b[5GThere are no traders or AI in the hosted world yet; W10 adds NPC jobs.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B \u001b[3GSo running the economy less often would save at most\u001b[56Gabout 5%.\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[1mSame results in fewer steps\u001b[22m is pos\u001b[38Gible in pri\u001b[50Gciple, but not by giving systems thei\u001b[88G own rates. Her\u001b[104G,\u001b[106G\"\u001b[108Ghe s\u001b[113Gme\"\u001b[117Ghas\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bto\u001b[6Gmean bit-identical:\u001b[26Greplay\u001b[33Gacross\u001b[40Gbuilds,\u001b[48Gsaves\u001b[54Gand\u001b[58Gthe\u001b[62Gserver\u001b[69Gall\u001b[73Gassume\u001b[80Ga\u001b[82Gworld\u001b[88Gstepped\u001b[96GN\u001b[98Gtimes\u001b[104Gis\u001b[107Gexactly\u001b[115Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bsame world, and \u001b[20Ghe pinned world hashes check it. A system run less often only matches if it is a \u001b[102Gure fun\u001b[110Gtion\u001b[115Gof\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Btime across the\u001b[19Ggap\u001b[23Git\u001b[26Gskips.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  What would work is a \u001b[1mfast-forward over quiet steps\u001b[22m. Each system says when it next needs a step (a batch due,\u001b[112Gan\u001b[115Gorder\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bexpiring, a\u001b[15Gjourney\u001b[23Gending,\u001b[31Ga\u001b[33Gcontact\u001b[41Gpossible).\u001b[52GWhile\u001b[58Gnothing\u001b[66Gbut\u001b[70Gmotion\u001b[77Gby\u001b[80Gformula\u001b[88Gis\u001b[91Ghappening\u001b[101G(orbits,\u001b[110Grails,\u001b[117Ga\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcruise\u001b[10Gplaced\u001b[17Gby\u001b[20Gits\u001b[24Gtime),\u001b[31Gthe\u001b[35Gworld\u001b[41Gjumps\u001b[47Gstraight\u001b[56Gto\u001b