[0.129, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BWhat would work is a \u001b[1mfast-forward over quiet steps\u001b[22m. Each system says whe\u001b[77Git\u001b[80Gnext need\u001b[91Ga st\u001b[96Gp (a\u001b[101Gbatch due, an order\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bexp\u001b[7Gring, a journey ending\u001b[31Ga contact\u001b[41Gpossible). W\u001b[54Gile nothi\u001b[64Gg but motion by formula is happening (orb\u001b[106Gts, rai\u001b[114Gs, a\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcruise placed by its t\u001b[26Gme), the world jumps straight to\u001b[59Gthe next such\u001b[73Gst\u001b[76Gp. Most of a 4.49-day cruise is ex\u001b[111Gctly that.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BT\u001b[7Gc\u001b[9Gtch is that physics, docks and buggies would\u001b[54Geach have to prove\u001b[73Gthey're qu\u001b[84Get, \u001b[89Gr be placed by formula\u001b[112Gacross\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe\u001b[7Ggap.\u001b[12GThat\u001b[17Gis\u001b[20Ga\u001b[22Greal\u001b[27Gengine\u001b[34Gdesign\u001b[41Gwith\u001b[46Gits\u001b[50Gown\u001b[54Gdeterminism\u001b[66Gtests,\u001b[73Gnot\u001b[77Gsomething\u001b[87Gto\u001b[90Gslip\u001b[95Ginto\u001b[100GL26.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mMy recommendation:\u001b[22m finish L26 as it stands (the 2× f\u001b[56Gx, the \u001b[64Gliced an\u001b[73G stoppable\u001b[84Gstep, the budget\u001b[101Gtest). Then queu\u001b[118G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe fast-forward as a\u001b[25Gsepara\u001b[32Ge item: an\u001b[43Gengine item in Jettison's roadmap w\u001b[80Gh\u001b[82Ga\u001b[84Gre-entry\u001b[93Gtask\u001b[98Gin\u001b[101GManifest's\u001b[112Gdelivery\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Border,\u001b[10Gdecided\u001b[18Gbefore\u001b[25GW10's\u001b[31Gtraders\u001b[39Gadd\u001b[43Gmore\u001b[48Gper-step\u001b[57Gwork.\u001b[63GShould\u001b[70GI\u001b[72Gqueue\u001b[78Git?\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BThe \u001b[8Gngine \u001b[15Gat\u001b[19Gis\u001b[22Gstill running. Once it passes, I'll\u001b[58Gcommit\u001b[65Gthe\u001b[69Gengine\u001b[76G