[0.030, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mSame results in fewer steps\u001b[22m is pos\u001b[38Gible in principle, but not by giving \u001b[76Gystems their own rates. H\u001b[102Gre, \"the same\" has\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bto mean bit-iden\u001b[20Gical: r\u001b[28Gplay acros\u001b[39G builds, saves and \u001b[59Ghe\u001b[62Gserver all assume a\u001b[82Gworld \u001b[89Gtepped\u001b[96GN times is exactly\u001b[115Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bsa\u001b[8Gwo\u001b[11Gld,\u001b[15Gand\u001b[19Gthe\u001b[23Gpinned world\u001b[36Ghashes\u001b[43Gcheck\u001b[49Git.\u001b[53GA\u001b[55Gsystem\u001b[62Grun\u001b[66Gless\u001b[71Goften\u001b[77Gonly\u001b[82Gmatches\u001b[90Gif\u001b[93Git\u001b[96Gis\u001b[99Ga\u001b[101Gpure\u001b[106Gfunction\u001b[115Gof\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Btime\u001b[8Gacross\u001b[15Gthe\u001b[19Ggap\u001b[23Git\u001b[26Gskips.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BWhat would work is a \u001b[1mfast-forward over quiet steps\u001b[22m. Each system says whe\u001b[77Git\u001b[80Gnext need\u001b[91Ga st\u001b[96Gp (a\u001b[101Gbatch due, an order\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bexp\u001b[7Gring, a journey ending\u001b[31Ga contact\u001b[41Gpossible). W\u001b[54Gile nothi\u001b[64Gg but motion by formula is happening (orb\u001b[106Gts, rai\u001b[114Gs, a\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bcruise placed by its t\u001b[26Gme), the world jumps straight to\u001b[59Gthe next such\u001b[73Gst\u001b[76Gp. Most of a 4.49-day cruise is ex\u001b[111Gctly that.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BT\u001b[7Gc\u001b[9Gtch is that physics, docks and buggies would\u001b[54Geach have to prove\u001b[73Gthey're qu\u001b[84Get, \u001b[89Gr be placed by formula\u001b[112Gacross\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe\u001b[7Ggap.\u001b[12GThat\u001b[17Gis\u001b[20Ga\u001b[22Greal\u001b[27Gengine\u001b[34Gdesign\u001b[41Gwith\u001b[46Gits\u001b[50Gown\u001b[54Gdeterminism\u001b[66Gtests,\u001b[73Gnot\u001b[77Gsomething\u001b[87Gto\u001b[90Gslip\u001b[95Ginto\u001b[100GL26.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u00