1b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bt\u001b[7Gg\u001b[9Gp. That is a real engine design with its own\u001b[54Gdeterminism tests,\u001b[73Gnot someth\u001b[84Gng t\u001b[89G slip into L26.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mMy recommendation:\u001b[22G\u001b[22mfinish\u001b[29GL26\u001b[33Gas\u001b[36Git\u001b[39Gstands\u001b[46G(the\u001b[51G2×\u001b[54Gfix,\u001b[59Gthe\u001b[63Gsliced\u001b[70Gand\u001b[74Gstoppable\u001b[84Gstep,\u001b[90Gthe\u001b[94Gbudget\u001b[101Gtest).\u001b[108GThen\u001b[113Gqueue\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe fast-forward as a separate item: an engine item \u001b[56Gn Jetti\u001b[64Gon's roa\u001b[73Gmap with a\u001b[84Gre-entry task in\u001b[101GManifest's deliv\u001b[118Gry\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Border, decided before\u001b[25GW10's \u001b[32Graders add\u001b[43Gmore per-step work. Should I queue \u001b[80G?\u001b[82G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BThe\u001b[7Gengine\u001b[14Ggate\u001b[19Gis\u001b[22Gstill\u001b[28Grunning.\u001b[37GOnce\u001b[42Git\u001b[45Gpasses,\u001b[53GI'll\u001b[58Gcommit\u001b[65Gthe\u001b[69Gengine\u001b[76Gfix,\u001b[81Gmove\u001b[86GManifest's\u001b[97Gpin,\u001b[102Gmeasure\u001b[110Gthe\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bbudg\u001b[8Gt's fi\u001b[15Gur\u001b[19Gon\u001b[22Gan idle machine, and run \u001b[76G\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
