[0.037, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[6G\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  \u001b[39mAdded \u001b[1m11\u001b[22m lines\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 76 \u001b[22m   player's event sends as that player, an NPC's as that NPC, and no client or script can name\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m 77 \u001b[22m   another player or an NPC. It also reaches a `Sim::Controller` nested inside a command's fields,\u001b[K\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B\u001b[2m78\u001b[13G\u001b[22mwhich\u001b[19Gthe\u001b[23Ghost\u001b[28Gdoes\u001b[33Gnot\u001b[37Gyet\u001b[41Gstamp.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 79 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m- **A fast-forward over quiet steps** (the user's, 2026-11-20, after Manifest's L26): a cruising       \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 80 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  step of Manifest's is 13 µs, nearly all of it the engine's movement (Jolt's update of each frame's   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 81 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  world, the docks and their buggies, the spatial index, the cruise's placing) and under 5% the        \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 82 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  game's, so a 4.49-day cruise is 23 million steps of motion a formula could place. Each system says   \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 83 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  the next step it must run at (a batch due, an order lapsing, a journey ending, a contact             \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 84 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  possible), and the world, while nothing but motion by formula is under way (orbits, rails, a         \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m 85 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  cruise placed by its time), goes straight to the soonest, to the same bits as stepping there:        \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m     \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 86 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  physics, the docks and the buggies each prove themselves quiet or are placed in closed form over     \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 87 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  the gap. It changes what a system tells the step, so it is dearer the more systems there are:        \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 88 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  decided before Manifest's W10 adds traders' and NPC jobs' work to every step. Tested by a world      \u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   \u001b[38;2;80;200;80m\u001b[48;2;2;40;0m 89 +\u001b[38;2;248;248;242m  fast-forwarded and one stepped reaching the same state hash, the pinned hashes holding.              \r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[39m\u001b[2m 90 \r\u001b[1B\u001b[22m \u001b[3G   \u001b[2m 91 \u001b[11G\u001b[22m### Next: what the\u001b[30Ggame's\u001b[37Gnext\u001b[42Gslices\u001b[49Gstand\u001b[55Gon\r\u001b[1B     \u001b[2m 92 \u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[52C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m· 19m 31s\u001b[63G· ↓\u001b[39m \u001b[38;2;153;153;153m55.7k\u001b[73Gtokens)\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[20C\u001b[6B\u001b[38;2;0;204;204m1\u001b[38G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m · esc to inter\u001b[54Gupt · ← 1 agent · ↓ to manage\u001b[39m\u001b[K\u001b[27;1H\u001b[24;3H\u001b[?25h"]
